    "**ADAM ID: **[sm\\_us7000ttvf](https://api.adam.geospatial.wfp.org/api/collections/adam.adam_eq_events/items?uid=sm_us7000ttvf) Magnitude 5.4 earthquake at 10.0 depth occurred on Oct 29 2026 4km NW of Maewo Island. The epicentre of the earthquake was located at latitude -15.1213 longitude 168.0994. It impacted 11987 people within 50km. WFP’s Automated Disaster Analysis and Mapping (ADAM) system is an operational system for collecting, analysing and mapping geospatial and socio-economic information following sudden onset humanitarian emergencies."
